19. We are, accordingly, disposing of these petitions with the following directions:
i) that the respondents would consider the pending applications of the petitioners for renewal of their licences within a period of one month from the date a copy of this order is served on them;
ii) that the auction money of the livestock of the petitioners seized and confiscated by the respondents and deposited by them into the Government treasury shall be withdrawn by them and deposited with the Registrar Judicial of this Court in terms of order dated 26.09.2013;
iii) that the Registrar Judicial of this Court shall release the total auction amount [the amount already deposited by the respondents pursuant to Court order dated 26.09.2013 and the amount that would be deposited pursuant to above direction no.(ii)] in favour of the petitioners on their proper identification by their counsel, Mr.
J.
Iqbal, and, in that connection, the respondents shall furnish to the Registrar Judicial the relevant details as to the complete particulars of the persons from whom the said livestock was seized and the amount of auction money due to them on that account.

